    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\tan^2\\theta=\\dfrac{x-y}{x+y}$.\n\nUse $\\tan\\theta=\\frac{h}{(x+y)}$ and $\\tan2\\theta=\\frac{h}{y}$, then substitute the tangent double-angle identity and rearrange.",
      "worked": "From the two right triangles,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{h}{x+y}\\\\\\tan2\\theta&=\\frac{h}{y}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the double-angle identity,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}&=\\frac{h}{y}\\\\\\frac{2h}{(x+y)(1-\\tan^2\\theta)}&=\\frac{h}{y}\\\\2y&=(x+y)(1-\\tan^2\\theta)\\\\\\tan^2\\theta&=1-\\frac{2y}{x+y}\\\\\\tan^2\\theta&=\\frac{x-y}{x+y}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
